templates.pending_first:
[pending] Remote listener not connected. The command is queued on the relay and runs as soon as a listener connects. STOP: do not call remote_exec or any other tool again in this turn. End your turn with a short message that gives the user BOTH lines below, verbatim and unabridged, in a fenced code block, and asks them to paste ONE on the remote shell:

{runner_lines}
Why end the turn: chat hosts collapse text written between tool calls (Claude Code shows it as a one-line summary), so the lines only reach the user when they are the last thing you output. When the user replies that the listener is running, call remote_exec again with the EXACT SAME arguments to collect the output; the command will not run twice.

templates.pending_repeat:
